SUMMARY:[Beginner (& More) Hiking/ Adventure Group - SLC] Hard Hike: Frary Peak and Dooly Knob Trail
DESCRIPTION:Hard Hike: Frary Peak and Dooly Knob Trail\n\nLength: 7.9 miles \nElevation Gain: ~2\,400 ft\n\nLet’s hike to Frary Peak\, the tallest point on Antelope Island! We will also take a small detour to Dooly Knob\, a small peak along the way. \n\nThe lower elevation and lack of shade make this a great hike to do during the colder months and the bugs that the island is usually notorious for die off by this time of year. Antelope Island has such a unique landscape and the bison are very cool to witness\, so this is one of my favorite trails. My favorite part is the scramble just before the summit\, but it can be easily bypassed. \n\nIt will be chilly and windy\, so please come prepared with a jacket\, beanie\, gloves\, etc. Please also be prepared with plenty of water and snacks/food. \n\nThe trailhead is about an hour drive from SLC and there is a fee required to enter Antelope Island State Park\, so we can coordinate carpooling the week of the hike. There is a required $15 day-use fee per vehicle. \n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions!\n\nAllTrails Link:\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/custom-route-72a2bd8\n\nGroup: Beginner (& More) Hiking/ Adventure Group - SLC\nImage: https://i.groupme.com/2695x2477.jpeg.fbb7966607f3416da300873df1f52ffe
LOCATION:Frary Peak Trailhead\, 40.99394\, -112.20258
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
